sentences.text:
After perusal of record and hearing submissions on behalf of both the sides this court is of the view that in order to bring home guilt of the accused for the offences U/s 120-B IPC, Section 419/420 r/w Section 120-B IPC and 12(1)
(a) & (b) of PP Act r/w Section 120-B IPC, the prosecution was required to prove the following facts;
(i) That the accused Upkar Singh had taken an amount of Rs.9 Lakh and arranged the journey of the Juvenile in conflict with law Mandeep Singh by arranging passport on the basis of furnishing forged particulars/documents to the RPO.
